.TH UDECK-TERMINAL 1 "2026-11-06" "uDeck Terminal 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
udeck-terminal \- button-first Qt terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udeck-terminal
.RI [ --new-window ]
.RI [ --working-directory " DIR" ]
.RI [ -T " TITLE" ]
.RI [ -e " PROGRAM ARG..." ]
.br
.B udeck-terminal --
.I PROGRAM ARG...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs an independent Qt Quick terminal with one PTY per tab. Plain invocation
activates the most recent window in the same graphical session. An explicit
directory, title, command or --new-window creates a new window. Tasks continue
when switching to the desktop. Closing a session requires confirmation and
terminates its processes. Application exit does not preserve running tasks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --new-window
Create a new window.
.TP
.BI --working-directory " DIR"
Use DIR. The default is the caller's current working directory.
.TP
.BI -T " TITLE"
Set the new window's initial tab title.
.TP
.BI -e " PROGRAM ARG..."
Execute the remaining arguments directly, without a shell or variable expansion.
.TP
.B --
Treat the remaining arguments as the program and its arguments.
.TP
.B --doctor
Print read-only JSON diagnostics. Never prints session contents or environments.
.SH KEYS
Ctrl+Shift+T/W creates/closes a tab. Ctrl+Shift+C/V copies/pastes.
Ctrl+Shift+F searches literal text. Ctrl+Shift+M opens the menu.
Physical A sends Return, B sends Escape, X opens the menu, Y opens settings.
L/R selects the previous/next tab without wrapping. Ordinary keyboard letters,
Escape, function keys and page keys remain available to terminal applications.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/udeck/terminal.json
stores appearance preferences only. No transcripts or passwords are persisted
by the terminal. Programs running inside the terminal may maintain their own
history and configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR udeck-terminal-default (1),
.BR xdg-terminal-exec (1),
.BR update-alternatives (1)
